{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny","id":1417768,"title":"Can Sidereals just quit the Bureau of Destiny?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-11T21:35:47-07:00","id":1417768,"title":"Can Sidereals just quit the Bureau of Destiny?","content":"I'm sorry if this has been brought up before or has an older thread. I was reading the Histories of Betrayal side bar in Fangs at the Gate and noticed the words &quot;resigned from the Bureau of Destiny&quot; (pg 49). I know new addition and new themes. I guess I'm too used to earlier editions ideas. Though this does seem to let Sidereal characters actually act independently of Yu-Shan without filling out paper work for time off or having working vacations. Again sorry if this has been brought up before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/559-promeathen","name":"Promeathen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T22:10:14-07:00","id":1417770,"title":"","content":"In earlier editions they were called &quot;Ronin&quot; Sidereals, because they abandoned their duties. They weren't hunted or anything, to my knowledge, but they also didn't have the protection or authority of Heaven. And of course, if you're a Sidereal that's quit the Bureau because you didn't agree with their goals, you might end up crossing them and facing criminal charges down the line.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, but I wouldn't be surprised if we move to a less exotic term than &quot;ronin&quot; in Ex3.<br /> <br /> Edit: And, of course, corrupt gods and Sidereals might try to charge you anyway even if you've done nothing wrong. But Sidereals are precious and long-lived enough that I'd imagine the Bureau usually offers honey rather than vinegar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T00:03:12-07:00","id":1417775,"title":"","content":"They can also be booted out for a big enough transgression (cf. Rakan Thulio).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:25:48-07:00","id":1417967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1417770#post1417770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In earlier editions they were called &quot;Ronin&quot; Sidereals, because they abandoned their duties. They weren't hunted or anything, to my knowledge, but they also didn't have the protection or authority of Heaven. And of course, if you're a Sidereal that's quit the Bureau because you didn't agree with their goals, you might end up crossing them and facing criminal charges down the line.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure, but I wouldn't be surprised if we move to a less exotic term than &quot;ronin&quot; in Ex3.<br /> <br /> Edit: And, of course, corrupt gods and Sidereals might try to charge you anyway even if you've done nothing wrong. But Sidereals are precious and long-lived enough that I'd imagine the Bureau usually offers honey rather than vinegar.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've used &quot;rogue&quot; sidereals well enough as a term for the last editions with no issue. Clearer even, i'd say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:35:36-07:00","id":1417969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1417775#post1417775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can also be booted out for a big enough transgression (cf. Rakan Thulio).</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall Rakan was supposed to be getting killed for his transgressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T18:39:51-07:00","id":1417971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1417775#post1417775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They can also be booted out for a big enough transgression (cf. Rakan Thulio).</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that if you get to that point you don't &quot;boot them out&quot;, you kill them and make sure their next life is a better one. Now if they escape and hide and decide to use an ancient tool of the Gods to fuck you up...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T19:23:05-07:00","id":1417978,"title":"","content":"I think it's not implausible for the Bureau of Destiny to sometimes punish with exile rather than death, internally with a logic of wanting somebody away from the decision making processes and levers of power but where they haven't done something that warrants execution and might still provide good service in future, or even deserve some respect our leniency for prior service.<br /> <br /> Primarily to create compelling scenarios of that Sidereal being called in for some kind of job off the books or getting back into Heaven's good graces, or else encountering them in the wilderness with a more complex relationship with their peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-12T21:33:02-07:00","id":1417988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1417967#post1417967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I've used &quot;rogue&quot; sidereals well enough as a term for the last editions with no issue. Clearer even, i'd say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's certainly my first choice. We'll see what the devs say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-13T01:13:45-07:00","id":1417998,"title":"","content":"On a complete aside, does anyone know if the devs intent to do anything with those mission and fate snarl tables from 1e Sidereals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T08:54:44-07:00","id":1418198,"title":"","content":"Random quest tables are neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T16:21:07-07:00","id":1418263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1417978#post1417978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's not implausible for the Bureau of Destiny to sometimes punish with exile rather than death, internally with a logic of wanting somebody away from the decision making processes and levers of power but where they haven't done something that warrants execution and might still provide good service in future, or even deserve some respect our leniency for prior service.<br /> <br /> Primarily to create compelling scenarios of that Sidereal being called in for some kind of job off the books or getting back into Heaven's good graces, or else encountering them in the wilderness with a more complex relationship with their peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if it's somebody who's gonna get better in 10-20-50-100 years. But if we're talking about someone like Rakan Thulio who has really fucked it up, I don't see him getting another chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T00:35:25-07:00","id":1418311,"title":"","content":"I have no issues with the word &quot;ronin&quot; and the social connotations and expectations of a Sidereal aren't incongruous with a samurai. They fit the bill as water folk.<br /> <br /> But it is weird that DeathKNIGHTS go rogue but the AGENTS of Heaven become ronin. It really should be the other way around. Rogue Agent and Ronin Knight fit sooo much better. (And Deathknights fealty to a Deathlord, which 3E is tweaking, sure, fits better.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T00:41:06-07:00","id":1418312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1417988#post1417988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's certainly my first choice. We'll see what the devs say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rogue makes a lot more sense to me. As John Doe says, secret agents often 'go rogue' when they turn their back on their agencies and stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T03:03:00-07:00","id":1418327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1418263#post1418263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, if it's somebody who's gonna get better in 10-20-50-100 years. But if we're talking about someone like Rakan Thulio who has really fucked it up, I don't see him getting another chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not saying that there's never death.<br /> <br /> I would expect some exiles to be basically permanent. Not for the people trying to break down the whole divine order.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T10:08:38-07:00","id":1418388,"title":"","content":"&quot;Ronin&quot; is also used to refer to an unemployed person with a white-collar business background in modern Japan, which lines up somewhat with the bureaucratic nature of Yu-Shan","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T11:07:37-07:00","id":1418395,"title":"","content":"1E, at least, drew a distinction between Sidereals who were playing hooky, and those who had never even been inprocessed. <br /> <br /> According to Exalted: The Sidereals (pg 84) &quot;Other Sidereal Rogues are simply criminals who have turned their backs on their duty and on Creation for their own selfish ends. This tiny handful are regarded as criminals and are hunted by their fellow Sidereals. However, unless these beings are particularly disruptive, they can run for quite some time. Sidereals do not shed Sidereal blood lightly, and any attempt to assassinate a criminal could just as easily result in the assassin's death, so those criminals not a direct menace to the Celestial Order are generally left to themselves. After a few centuries, boredom and proffered amnesties bring most minor criminals back.&quot;<br /> <br /> And &quot;Rarer even than criminals are Ronin, Sidereals who have never been trained as part of the Five-Score Fellowship. Sometimes these Exalted come into being due to the direct intervention of the Maidens. Others are young Exalted who are not contacted by the Celestial Bureaucracy for years on end due to bureaucratic error or lack of resources.&quot;<br /> <br /> So a Sidereal who leaves the Bureau is a Rogue. A Sidereal who has never served is a Ronin, probably because no Sidereal can be sure they aren't serving at the specific desire of a Maiden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 10-15-2020, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-20T13:58:35-07:00","id":1419223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1418388#post1418388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Ronin&quot; is also used to refer to an unemployed person with a white-collar business background in modern Japan, which lines up somewhat with the bureaucratic nature of Yu-Shan</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Uh, kind of, but not quite, actually. If memory tricks me not - and i admit i'm far from a specialist - the term is usually associated with young people that are between high school &amp; college exploring their options in search for their own place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-21T12:43:25-07:00","id":1419415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/1417768-can-sidereals-just-quit-the-bureau-of-destiny?p=1418311#post1418311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no issues with the word &quot;ronin&quot; and the social connotations and expectations of a Sidereal aren't incongruous with a samurai. They fit the bill as water folk.<br /> <br /> But it is weird that DeathKNIGHTS go rogue but the AGENTS of Heaven become ronin. It really should be the other way around. Rogue Agent and Ronin Knight fit sooo much better. (And Deathknights fealty to a Deathlord, which 3E is tweaking, sure, fits better.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't mind the current terminology, because the Underworld (and Abyssals by extension) always seemed to me to be the one facet of Exalted that was more inspired by western fiction/myth than Eastern stuff. So Abyssals get called Death<i>knights</i> because they are often the closest thing to a true Western European knight in the setting--in the 3e core, what Abyssals we see in art often are very clearly in European-style plate armor (especially that unhelmeted guy holding a rise in the Antagonists section that looks like he came right out of a medieval fantasy book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}